## Filament Image Annotations (asignua/filament-image-annotations)

- Non-destructive markup over an image (arrow, rectangle, ellipse, line, pen, highlighter, text). The file is never touched; the layer is JSON in the `image_annotations` table (publish with `--tag=filament-image-annotations-migrations`, then `migrate` and `filament:assets`). The service provider is auto-discovered; `ImageAnnotationsPlugin` on the panel is optional.
- Every entry point takes `->image($x)`: an `ImageSource`, a Spatie `Media`, a class registered with `app(ImageSources::class)->register(Foo::class, fn (Foo $f) => new FooSource($f))`, or a Closure returning one (`null` hides the button).
- Editor in a modal: `AnnotateImageAction::make()->image(fn (Post $record) => $record->getFirstMedia('photos'))` (table row, header or infolist action). Read-only: `AnnotatedImageEntry::make('photo')->image(...)` in infolists, `<x-image-annotations::image :image="$media" alt="..." />` anywhere (needs Alpine + Filament assets, otherwise a plain image). Form field: `ImageAnnotator::make('annotations')->image(...)`; saving it is up to you (`ImageAnnotations::store()->save($source, $user, $state)`).
- Uploads: wrap them, `AnnotatedUpload::make(FileUpload::make('image')->image()->disk('public'))` or with `SpatieMediaLibraryFileUpload`. It returns a state-less `Group` (upload + list as siblings), configure the upload BEFORE wrapping. Only stored images get an enabled button (not on a create page, not a fresh upload); annotating saves immediately, not with the form's Save. For a plain `FileUpload` the layer is keyed by the file path on the record and is forgotten when the file is removed and the record saved.
- Sources: `Sources\MediaImageSource($media)` (key null), `Sources\ModelPathImageSource($record, $path, $disk)` (key = path). A model whose image is a path in a column should use the `HasImageAnnotations` trait (rows removed on `forceDelete()` only). Media deletion removes its layer automatically. Use `::urlUsing(Closure)` on a source for signed/CDN URLs (private disks).
- Authorization: guests never; a signed-in user needs `view` / `update` on the owner model's policy; WITH NO POLICY any signed-in user may view and annotate. Override once with `ImageAnnotations::authorizeUsing(fn (?Authenticatable $user, ImageSource $source, string $ability): bool => ...)` (`$ability` is `'view'` or `'annotate'`). `AnnotationStore::save()` throws `AuthorizationException` itself.
- Read from code: `ImageAnnotations::for($image)` (layer for the current user or null), `ImageAnnotations::store()->shapes/save/forget`. An empty layer deletes the row. Events: `AnnotationSaved`, `AnnotationDeleted`.
- Stored shape format `{"v":1,"items":[{id,type,pts:[[x,y],...],color,width,text?}]}` with coordinates normalised 0..1; always passed through `Support\ShapeSanitizer` (never throws). Text is stored raw and rendered with `textContent`, never inject it with `innerHTML` or `{!! !!}`.
- Config `filament-image-annotations.php`: `table`, `palette` (name => hex), `widths`, `limits` (`shapes`, `points`, `text`), `user_model`. v1 has ONE layer per image (any authorised user edits it, `user_id` = last editor); per-author layers and comment pins are a future Pro package.
